
@  T-29. 4.34: NOBODY IS RESCUED. The player arrives, and arriving is the
@  entire contribution. She is not surprised and she is not grateful, and the
@  first line is the one that says how long she has been here without saying
@  anything about how long she has been here.
BirthIsland_Exterior_Text_CrystalDoesNotAsk::
	.string "She does not ask how you got here.\p"
	.string "She looks at what you are holding.$"

@  8.2a: "She reads it. That is the last scene. What is in it is not written
@  here and may never need to be." So it is not written here either.
@
@  She turns it over, she asks one word, she walks to the water and opens it
@  facing away, and the script ENDS WITH HER STILL FACING AWAY. Craft rule 1's
@  hardest case: the loudest available last line is whatever is on that paper,
@  and the game does not have it.
BirthIsland_Exterior_Text_PayloadTurnedItOver::
	.string "CRYSTAL CLEAR turned the package\n"
	.string "over once and did not open it.\p"
	.string "She looked at the name on it for\n"
	.string "longer than reading it takes.$"

BirthIsland_Exterior_Text_PayloadWhere::
	.string "“…Where.”\p"
	.string "…\p"
	.string "“Thank you. That is all I needed\n"
	.string "to know.”$"
